WEBVTT

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.060
Yes, sir.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.670
I'd like to look at your greeting cards.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.490
Well, I'll show you our display counter, and you can pick one out for yourself.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.290
Blanche

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:18.750
Mm-hmm.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.990
They're showing our first television show of the season tonight,

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.390
so why don't you and Harry come over to our house and watch it with us?

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.720
Well, I'm, uh...

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:29.860
I'm afraid, George.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.620
may not like it. Oh, Blance, George seems to like our show better than anybody.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.260
What the hell?

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.530
Oh, I don't mean that.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.750
In fact, I've seen him laughing at our show

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.290
when you and Harry were yawning.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.200
If you're talking about last week, we hadn't had much sleep the night before.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.540
Say, Blanche.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.550
You know, I think it would be nice to have a party tonight.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.720
You know, it would be a lot more fun to watch the show

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.220
if all our friends were there to tell us how much they like it.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.980
Well, if-if George wants to know what people-

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.500
People think at the show, you don't invite friends, you invite strangers.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:04.680
I had some one.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:05.990
Oh

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.560
You're so clever.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.760
I'll be with you in just a minute, ma'am.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.500
Now then, let's see. Which one of you ladies came in first?

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:15.440
I did, but you can wait on her first.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:17.910
Oh, no, if you came in first, I'll take care of you first.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.610
All right, but you'll make less money that way

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.710
because I didn't come in here to buy anything she did.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:25.390
Thank you.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.220
We came in together.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:29.330
Thank you.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.200
Thank you very much.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.230
My husband would like a package of this ledger paper.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.510
Do you have it exactly like this sample?

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.180
Well...

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.910
Well, our stationary section's right over here.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:43.790
Oh, thank you.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:44.960
I hope.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.800
Wait a minute, mister. What are you doing tonight?

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:50.170
Tonight?

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.510
Yes, I'm giving a television party.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.570
Would you like to come?

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.640
Well, I hardly know what to say.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:56.920
We don't know each other.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.120
Well, that's perfect.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.960
You know, Blanche gave me a wonderful idea.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.920
I'm only inviting strangers.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.160
Here's my idea.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.200
Strangers?

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:05.660
Mm-hmm.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:06.990
Thank you.

00:02:07.276 --> 00:02:10.170
Well, uh, I'm afraid I couldn't go, you see.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.530
I'm short of help.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.900
My assistant's uncle died, and he went to Las Vegas.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:15.400
Oh.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:15.940
Oh!

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.220
minute you know this is no time for him to go he'll miss his own funeral

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.880
I mean, my assistant went to Las Vegas.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.580
Well, he'll miss the funeral, too.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:31.250
This is George Burns.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.990
Oh, there's the woman I don't know.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.390
Oh, Mrs. Burns.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.910
Yes, I'd like very much to come.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:36.890
Oh, good.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.530
And if your assistant and his uncle get back in time, bring him along.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:44.420
Hello.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.060
Hello.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.920
Why don't you come to my party at 8 o'clock tonight?

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.260
Oh, here's my address.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:52.200
Party?

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:52.840
Mm-hmm.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.440
Well, I don't think I've ever met you.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.360
You haven't.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.360
Well, then I wouldn't know anyone there.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.500
Oh, well, that's all right.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:02:59.720
Neither will anybody else.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.340
Mrs. George Burns.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.850
Oh, you're Gracie Allen.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.280
Well, I certainly will come.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.850
My husband and I watch you every week.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.450
He always says, how can any woman be that stupid?

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.770
Oh, well, don't feel bad.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.290
Husbands are all alike.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.850
You know, sometimes my husband says the same thing to me.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.580
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.960
wait a minute I want to talk to that man who is he well I don't know I'll

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:58.900
introduce him to you tonight oh hello oh I want you to come to my house to a

00:03:58.900 --> 00:03:59.880
television party tonight

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:06.000
night at eight o'clock. Oh, when that funeral is over in Las Vegas, don't forget to bring them.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:14.990
No, no, I won't. What was that? Oh, Blanche, I don't know how to thank you for that idea you

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:21.610
suggested. It's wonderful. I suggested something? Well, to invite strangers to our television party

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:28.760
tonight. And, you know, everybody I've invited so far has accepted. Oh, no, honey, I didn't mean

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:29.980
that? That wasn't my idea.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.990
Oh, you're too modest.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:35.990
Wait till George hears about it.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:37.960
But Gracie, I...

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.820
Oh, another stranger, man.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.020
Oh, no, Gracie.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:48.490
In a few hours, I'm going to watch our first television show of the new season.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.130
If you get a chance, I hope you'll watch it, too.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:55.720
You know, it's just like an opening night, and I'm really worried.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.970
You see, in show business, they say that all actors who have...

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:01.890
and get nervous on opening nights.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:06.670
Word.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.660
When I did a single in Vaudeville,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.300
I never got nervous on opening nights.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.460
I never even got nervous on closing nights.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.560
Come to think of it,

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.820
they were usually the same night.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.820
Two newspaper men over to watch our show tonight.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.700
Jack Hellman of Variety

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.580
and Leo Gild of the Hollywood Reporter

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:29.980
and the...

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:34.060
They give you good notice, it carries a lot of weight.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:38.360
It always hands me a laugh, the way other actors on opening night

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.680
wine them and dine them and buy them all kinds of presents

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.840
just to get on the right side of them, but not me.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:46.890
I do that every time I see them.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.350
You know, critics are not always right.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:55.110
When Jag Benny first went into the radio business, oh, about 25 years ago,

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:59.170
a certain critic in New York named Hemmendinger gave him a very bad notice.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:03.570
He said a man with so little talent will be forgotten in one year.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:04.810
But he was wrong.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.570
They forgot Hemendinger in about six months.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:13.180
You know, last year, we invited the Mortons over to watch our opening show,

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.520
and Blanche had an unusual kind of hay fever.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.350
She only sneezed during my monologue.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.530
And 20 minutes later, when I sang my song,

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.700
her husband started to say gesundheit.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.980
There were so many disturbances, I couldn't tell whether...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.450
the show was good or bad so the next day i went all over town asking people how they liked it

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:39.870
i asked the man who runs the filling station if he and his wife saw saw a show last night he said i'm

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:46.290
afraid not since we got a television set my wife and i don't go out much anymore on my way to the

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.990
flyers club i met a friend of mine bonnie darren and i says bonnie did you see our show last night

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:55.610
he says yes i said how'd you like it he said oh boy and kept walking i still don't know whether

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.070
it's old boy good or old boy bad.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:06:59.660
Well,

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.000
I'd better get things ready for Hellman and Guild.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.660
Our show should be going on at about...

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:17.600
I guess I have got talent.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:18.920
See, I am nervous.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.490
What's the favor you wanted to ask?

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:24.400
Oh, oh.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:27.060
Well, our first show of the new season goes tonight.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.260
Could I come over here and watch it with you?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:35.790
won't you hear it over at george's i assumed we'd all be invited as usual hadn't you heard about that

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:40.750
i know what oh well this year george has invited the television editors a variety and reporter

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:46.970
over to watch the show with him and nobody else oh i see doing a little apple polishing so he'll

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:52.880
get a good notice huh shame on it george wouldn't stoop to a thing like that just because he's sending

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:56.640
a limousine to pick them up and bought them dollar and a half cigars and some fine french

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.660
Cognac doesn't mean he has an ulterior motive.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:01.890
the same thing for anybody else who'd write him

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:02.530
a good notice.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:05.930
I had to hold

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:08.210
in my big mouth. Hey, Blanche's home.

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:09.990
Well, then, Harry, by all means, come over

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:11.910
here. I can understand why George doesn't

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.150
want to be disturbed. I don't know what's the matter with me.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.020
Just say something like, strangers

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.150
I knew that came from. Blanche, are you

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.610
sure you're well? Oh, yes.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.250
Come along, Mr. Bonneville.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.720
What a day I've had. Gracie

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.680
went shopping with me, and she was in great

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.760
form. Everywhere we went,

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.800
Every time she met a stranger, she invited them to come over to her house tonight.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.700
She's giving a television party.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:37.740
Are you kidding?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:43.870
Only the people we met in three stores and on the bus coming home.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.510
Well, I gotta talk to Gracie and stop that.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.550
George will blow his top.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:48.750
He certainly will.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:52.130
Yeah, you know, George is having two newspaper men over to the house tonight,

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.850
and he doesn't want anybody to disturb them.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:57.350
Oh, and I feel responsible.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:08:59.980
Golly, I hope Mr. Bonzel can...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.510
straighten it out well i'm not really interested did you get my ledger paper well of course what's

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:14.500
this oh that's a pound of my favorite coconut bonbons you like them too only when i can't get

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:20.690
shredded wheat dipped in mucilage is this the ledger paper no no no that's a pair of black

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:25.330
and white striped pajamas i bought at the may company i had the same kind five years ago remember

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:29.670
yeah so do all the neighbors a long time they thought i was living with a zebra

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:33.460
I can't find any ledger paper in here.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.820
Oh, you men are so helpless.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.200
You never can find anything.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.480
I'll get it.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:39.910
Ha-ha.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.550
How do you like that stupid clerk

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:46.060
he let me walk out and forget the paper?

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.320
But you didn't forget the bonbons

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.540
or the striped pajamas.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.450
Well, no.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.650
Obviously, your motto is,

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.450
if you can't eat it or wear it, forget it.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.370
Now, if your head was not attached

00:09:58.370 --> 00:09:59.970
to your spinal column, you'd forget...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.920
that too now you know i needed that ledger paper to complete an audit for the perkins bearing company

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:09.840
and yet you fail in the performance of this one simple task you think of nobody but yourself

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:19.230
you are utterly and completely inconsiderate and furthermore you you're the sweetest little zebra

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:28.560
i was ever married to hi gracie

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.650
Oh, Harry, I'm glad you came.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.150
I wanted to invite you to our television party tonight.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:36.450
Well, that's what I wanted to...

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.350
Oh, you know, dozens of people are coming over,

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.450
so I'm fixing the sandwiches now.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.550
Oh, would you mind getting me the Swiss cheese

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:43.470
